 "song": {
  "name": "concrete (meta)",
  "bpm": 134,
  "ticksPerBeat": 4,
  "length": 64,
  "loop": {
   "start": 0,
   "end": 64
  },
  "info": "Four bars of techno from five percussion machines (a kick, a hi-hat, a clap, a comb-resonator metal percussion and a tuned tom), all played by one meta machine. The grid lane has no notes of its own: each of its columns is a proxy of one thing of another machine, so the kick, hat, clap, metal and tom have no lanes at all. n1 v1 are the kick note and velocity, then its pitch envelope, pitch decay, decay and tune; t1 t2 the hat hits (closed, open) and its decays, tone and tune; t3 the clap and its tone, tail, bursts and spacing; n2 is the metal as a 2hex note relative to E-5 (80 is E-5, 83 is G-5, 87 is B-5, 00 would be a note off); n3 is the tom relative to C-3. The sound moves through the parameter columns. Each pattern is four rows and is placed again where the music repeats."
 },
